// P03.26: unsafe.Sizeof, Alignof and Offsetof of types nested by value (the struct shape at 70 and 1000 levels; sizeof-nest-all.long.test runs every shape at 70, 200 and 1000), and a wrong size given for generic instances is refused (so the checks are real).
// The sizes were worked out by a recursion that stopped at depth 64 and
// answered one word below it; they are now worked out with a stack of their
// own and a memo for every type (Checker::gcLayout), so there is no limit on
// the depth and a type that is used twice (`dag`) is worked out once. The
// numbers come from a model of the gc layout in Inputs/check-sizeof-nest.py,
// which sizeof-nest-go.long.test compares with `go run`.
// RUN: %python %S/Inputs/check-sizeof-nest.py %gopp %t.d gopp
// RUN: %python %S/Inputs/check-sizeof-nest.py %gopp %t.d wrong
